{"v":1,"st":"TX","y":"2020","L":{"cd":{"f":"2020-cd.json","n":36,"lbl":"U.S. House","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_us_cd116_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_us_cd116_500k.zip","35113ca7612b14333bfbf24ec074d01278bc8ea13d836213b1c7390ba945c830"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's lines of the 116th Congress's districts (its file says session 116). The Bureau published no file of the 117th Congress's districts, the Congress the 2020 election chose.","chk":[36,36,0],"why":"","rec":["Plan C235 (S.B. 4, 83rd Legislature, 1st Called Session, 2013): the three-judge court's 2012 interim plan, adopted unchanged as the permanent plan; 36 districts","2012-05-29","Texas Legislature Online: S.B. 4, 83rd Leg., 1st C.S. (2013), bill history (signed 2013-06-26)","https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=831&Bill=SB4","Signed 2013-06-26, effective 2013-09-24; used in every congressional election from 2012 through 2020. Census file: the Bureau's user note says its products hold the 116th Congress and the 2018 election-year legislative lines and none of the later changes; the cached cb_2020 files carry CDSESSN 116 / LSY 2018. Cached files: cb_2020 cd116 holds 36 Texas districts, cb_2022 and cb_2024 hold 38, and none of the 36 shares a shape with them."],"c":36,"lv":{"federal":36}},"sldu":{"f":"2020-sldu.json","n":31,"lbl":"State Senate","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_us_sldu_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_us_sldu_500k.zip","5fcedd3ac126a22d9beaefda04abf217f27bc29e1f515a7255b1c3b6c13bb594"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's 2020 file of legislative districts, the lines it records for the 2018 legislative session year. The Bureau published no file of the lines in use for 2020. Where a state's lines changed in between, the check below or the plan cited stops the map.","chk":[15,15,0],"why":"","rec":["Plan S172 (S.B. 2, 83rd Legislature, 1st Called Session, 2013): the court's 2012 interim Senate plan, adopted as the permanent plan; 31 districts","2012-05-29","Texas Legislature Online: S.B. 2, 83rd Leg., 1st C.S. (2013), bill history (signed 2013-06-26)","https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=831&Bill=SB2","Signed 2013-06-26, effective immediately; the bill's own text says the plan was used to elect the Senate in 2012. No court change to the Senate plan before 2020. Census file: the Bureau's user note says its products hold the 116th Congress and the 2018 election-year legislative lines and none of the later changes; the cached cb_2020 files carry CDSESSN 116 / LSY 2018."],"c":15,"lv":{"legislature":15}},"sldl":{"f":"","n":0,"lbl":"State House","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_us_sldl_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_us_sldl_500k.zip","cac23d32db3b74bb50ca5e02e085cf75dcd4ec20f754aad5bea3aae0a3985031"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's 2020 file of legislative districts, the lines it records for the 2018 legislative session year. The Bureau published no file of the lines in use for 2020. Where a state's lines changed in between, the check below or the plan cited stops the map.","chk":[115,115,0],"why":"No map of Texas's lower chamber districts for 2020: the election was held on the Plan H358 (S.B. 3, 83rd Legislature, 1st Called Session, 2013), as modified for the 2020 elections by court-ordered Plan H411 in House District 90 and the adjoining Tarrant County districts (order of 2019-05-28); 150 districts, and the Census Bureau published no file of those lines, so this page draws none. The official record of the plan is under The lines.","rec":["Plan H358 (S.B. 3, 83rd Legislature, 1st Called Session, 2013), as modified for the 2020 elections by court-ordered Plan H411 in House District 90 and the adjoining Tarrant County districts (order of 2019-05-28); 150 districts","2020-03-03","Texas Legislature Online: S.B. 3, 83rd Leg., 1st C.S. (2013), bill history (signed 2013-06-26)","https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=831&Bill=SB3","H358 was signed 2013-06-26 (effective 2013-09-24) and first used in the 2014-03-04 primary (the 2012 House plan was the court's interim H309). After Abbott v. Perez (2018-06-25) held HD 90 a racial gerrymander, the three-judge court ordered H358 modified by H411 'to elect members of the Texas House of Representatives in the 2020 elections'. The order's text does not list the districts H411 changes (they are in its exhibits): the order says HD 90 and adjoining districts in Tarrant County, and no other change to H358. The Census 2020 file is the 2018 lines (LSY 2018; the Bureau's products carry no change made after the 2018 election), so HD 90 and its Tarrant County neighbours are drawn in the file as in H358 before the remedy. Everywhere else the file matches. used_from is the 2020 primary, the first election held with H411's lines."]},"place":{"f":"2020-place.json","n":90,"lbl":"Cities, towns and villages","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_us_place_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_us_place_500k.zip","0d177eb93798cfbc88cdcbafed401dc0a3e6d9b062f80a3d431d4f903a0fc0e4"]],"vint":"The Census Bureau's 2020 file (boundaries as of January 1, 2020).","chk":[],"why":"","c":380,"lv":{"city":206,"measure":174}},"sd":{"f":"2020-sd.json","n":55,"lbl":"School districts","src":[["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_us_unsd_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_us_unsd_500k.zip","74c876b9663129e9c6f1aff01a5ba716e389f9b476ba4f8184c5bccb627f6fa5"],["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_48_elsd_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_48_elsd_500k.zip","59c1e2693d1490a491ce0b14c02d6551cd8e0b300396f208997ff818ffd59686"],["U.S. Census Bureau, cartographic boundary file cb_2020_48_scsd_500k","https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2020/shp/cb_2020_48_s